Data and services in use today
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VIIRS Nighttime Lights (VNL) v2 annual composite, 2024
  Earth Observation Group, Payne Institute for Public Policy, Colorado School of Mines.
  https://eogdata.mines.edu/products/vnl/
  Used to derive the Astr zone data. EOG publishes many VNL products under CC BY 4.0; the exact licence of
  the product used here is to be confirmed against EOG's licence document.
  Cite: Elvidge, C.D., Zhizhin, M., Ghosh, T., Hsu, F.-C., Taneja, J. (2021). Annual time series of global
  VIIRS nighttime lights derived from monthly averages: 2012 to 2019. Remote Sensing 13(5), 922.

Weather data
  Weather data by Open-Meteo.com, licensed CC BY 4.0. https://open-meteo.com/
  Subject to Open-Meteo's terms of use. Free use is for non-commercial purposes; confirm that a free,
  open-source, tip-based app qualifies before the first store release.

H3 geospatial indexing
  Uber H3, Apache-2.0, through the h3_flutter package. https://h3geo.org/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Transitional dependency (not Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Swiss Ephemeris, through the sweph package
  Astrodienst AG (Dieter Koch and Alois Treindl). Licensed AGPL-3.0, or under a paid Professional License.
  https://www.astro.com/swisseph/
  The app currently depends on sweph. Binaries that include it are subject to the AGPL-3.0, which conflicts
  with distributing the whole app under Apache-2.0. It is being replaced by an implementation built on JPL
  ephemerides (decision D5). Do not publish a store build that includes sweph.

